messages[14]{user,text}:
  user_1,[00:00] Hey Anjali, it's Reyansh. I just... uh... wanted to double-check the policy expiration date. I think the new one runs till...?
  user_2,[00:15] Hi Reyansh! Yeah, sure—let me pull that up. The renewed policy is good through 30 Sept 2027.
  user_1,[00:30] Oh, okay, great. And the deductible is still $2,500, right? I saw that in the PDF.
  user_2,[00:35] Correct, $2,500 deductible, $150 monthly premium. Anything else on your mind?
  user_1,[00:45] Yeah, I was wondering—if I... uh... make a claim before the deductible, how does that work? Like, do I pay out‑of‑pocket first?
  user_2,[00:50] Basically, you pay up to the deductible amount before the insurer kicks in. After $2,500, we cover the rest per the policy terms.
  user_1,[01:00] Got it. And the tele‑consultation—does that cover... I mean, can I use it for a mental health specialist?
  user_2,[01:05] Yes, tele‑consult works for any specialist, including mental health. You just need to use our portal or the app.
  user_1,[01:15] Cool, cool. One more thing—if I need to cancel the policy later, what's the process? I know it's not my plan now, but just in case.
  user_2,[01:20] If you ever decide to cancel, just give us a 30‑day notice. We'll process any prorated refund. But since you're happy, no worries.
  user_1,[01:30] Thanks, Anjali. I appreciate the help. Anything else I should know?
  user_2,[01:35] Just remember to keep your policy documents handy and submit claims within 90 days. We're here if you need anything.
  user_1,[01:40] Will do. Thanks again! Bye.
  user_2,[01:45] Bye, Reyansh. Take care.